Added long-term retention for change and job history. Records older than a configurable warm window are moved into retained-history tables, one calendar period per record type, so the warm tables stay bounded without history being deleted at the cutoff.
Added the `changelog_archive` database connection alias, defaulting to the same physical database as `default` so retention needs no separate provisioning to enable. Repoint it with the `NAUTOBOT_CHANGELOG_ARCHIVE_DB_*` environment variables. `ChangelogArchiveRouter` pins the retained-history tables to that alias.
Added `ArchiveSegment`, which registers one calendar period per record type, and `ArchivedObjectChange`, `ArchivedJobResult`, `ArchivedJobLogEntry`, and `ArchivedJobConsoleEntry`, which hold the retained records.
Added the `Changelog Rotation` system job, which moves change and job history older than the warm window into the calendar period its own timestamp falls in. Rotation is idempotent: re-running files the same records in the same period without duplicating them.
Added validation refusing a retention rule for a model changelog retention does not cover, and an archive segment whose period ends at or before it starts. Both would otherwise save cleanly and then never behave: the rule would sit in the list looking enabled while truncation never walked its model, and the segment would make reconciliation report every record filed against it as outside its own period.
Added `RetentionRule`, a filter-driven model controlling what changelog truncation deletes, with UI and REST API CRUD, and the `Changelog Truncation` system job, which deletes warm change and job history selected by those rules in bounded increments, independently of whether rotation is configured.
Added the `Changelog Archive Integrity Check` and `Changelog Archive Reconciliation` system jobs, which stand in for the referential integrity the retained-history tables do not enforce. The first reports retained records whose referent no longer exists, and deletes them only when asked; the second verifies each period's recorded row count, that no record falls outside the period filing it, and that nothing exists in both warm storage and retention.
Added the `nautobot-server check_changelog_archive_schema` command and a matching startup check, which report retained-history tables that have fallen behind the models they mirror.
Added the `extras.view_archivesegment` permission as the single gate on reading retained history, excluded from `EXEMPT_VIEW_PERMISSIONS` handling so a global exemption cannot open it by accident.
Added a period selector to the change log list view and the object change log tabs, offering the retained periods a user is permitted to read. Selecting a period replaces the warm records with that period's, carries the current filters and sorting over, and shows how current the period is. Retained records are read-only, so row actions and bulk selection are not offered for them.
Added filtering within a retained period. The retained-history filtersets are derived from the warm ones, so the same query parameters apply; filters that traverse a relation the retained record holds as an identifier column are dropped, and `?changed_object_type=` continues to work against the identifier column.
Added object links to retained change records. The Object column on a retained list, and the Changed Object field on a retained record's detail page, link to the object the record describes when that object still exists, resolved from the identifier the record stores in one lookup per object type on the page. Records whose object has since been deleted show the recorded `object_repr` as plain text, as before.
Added retained records to the existing detail views: an archived object change or job result opens at the same URL it had before rotation, read-only, with its difference panel, previous and next change navigation, and related changes resolved within its period.
Added `?archive_period=` to the `/api/extras/object-changes/`, `/api/extras/job-results/`, and `/api/extras/job-logs/` list endpoints, which serves one period of retained history. Available values are discoverable from a read-only `/api/extras/archive-segments/` endpoint, also surfaced in the UI.
Added the `CHANGELOG_ARCHIVE_ENABLED`, `CHANGELOG_WARM_WINDOW_DAYS`, `CHANGELOG_ARCHIVE_PERIOD`, and `CHANGELOG_TRUNCATION_BATCH_SIZE` configuration settings.
Added a declared field contract between each retention mirror and the model it mirrors, asserting that every field is present on both, that fields not excepted are identical, and that the two kinds of permitted exception hold: a foreign key demoted to an identifier column, and a timestamp the mirror must not fill in for itself.
Added retained job history to the job result detail page's panels: the log table, the console output, the console export, and the log export link all serve a retained result, filtered and sorted within its period.
Added the custom field scope filter construct to retention rules: a rule's `scope_filter` is built with the same filter form, so it selects exactly what that filter selects in the change log. `ScopedFilterMixin` and `ScopedFilterViewMixin` are shared by both, in place of the two having separate implementations.
Changed the Changelog Truncation job to apply every enabled retention rule, with no per-run rule picker: the rule's own `enabled` field is the switch. It reports whether no rules exist or none are enabled, rather than a bare zero, since a run has nothing to apply in either case.
Added the `without_delete_change_logging()` context manager, which detaches the change log's delete receiver for a bulk deletion and guarantees it is reattached. The changelog cleanup, rotation, and truncation jobs use it in place of a hand-rolled try/finally each.
Added the `CHANGELOG_ROTATION_BATCH_SIZE` setting (default 1000), separate from the truncation batch size because rotation holds each record in memory to copy it while truncation needs only their keys.
Added the `nautobot-server create_changelog_retention_demo_data` command, which fabricates backdated change and job history, rotates it, and creates retention rules and two users differing only in the cold-storage permission, so long-term retention can be exercised on an instance that has no history old enough to rotate.
Added the `CHANGELOG_LEGACY_OBJECT_DATA` setting, controlling whether each change record stores the pre-1.3 `object_data` snapshot alongside `object_data_v2`. It defaults to `True`; turning it off halves what each new change record writes.
Added read-only detail views for archived object changes and job results, reachable from the rows of a retained period.
